This paper introduces a novel approach to deriving solutions for various equations by employing a new exponential Taylor expansion method. The author begins with a fundamental lemma that serves as the basis for this technique. Applications are provided to derive exponential solutions for the simple harmonic oscillator, the damped harmonic oscillator, and the single-particle Schrödinger equation involving a Gaussian wave packet. This methodology offers a straightforward alternative to traditional power series expansions. Additionally, the text examines a problem concerning the approximation of the natural logarithm of 2 using a standard power series and contrasts these findings with results obtained from the exponential Taylor expansion method. Furthermore, the text discusses the derivation of the normal distribution from the single-particle Schrödinger equation, contrasting the conventional approach with a new derivation utilizing the exponential Taylor expansion method. Finally, the work concludes with an appendix containing exercises for readers. The author hopes this paper will inspire others to develop new techniques for solving problems in physics and mathematics. Keywords: Exponential Taylor Expansion, Exponential Solution, Harmonic Oscillator, Gaussian Wave Packet, Normal Distribution.
